-- erwartet: C001
-- 1001 -- **`own@m`: a form the grammar admits and no side of the compiler answers for.**
--
-- `parse::right` reads `own [ "@" ident ]` and builds `Recht::Eigen(Some(marke))`.
-- **That line is the last one in the repository that looks inside the `Some`.**
-- Measured 2026-09-15:
--
--     grep -rn "Eigen(Some" crates/    ->  parse.rs:1418, and nothing else
--
-- Every other reader -- `m3.rs` twice, `alias.rs`, `lean_g.rs` twice, `emit.rs` --
-- matches `Recht::Eigen(_)` and drops the mark on the floor. So:
--
--   * `ptr<normal, own@m> u32` and `ptr<normal, own> u32` emit the SAME C to the byte,
--   * they book the same obligations (none),
--   * and no pass refuses either of them.
--
-- **The specification has no constructor for it either.** `Ty.ptr` in
-- `grammatik/Grammatik/Syntax.lean` carries `(t : Nat)` and `(rw : Bool)` -- a
-- target and a write bit, and no mark.
--
-- The corpus asks for the form ZERO times (`grep -rn "own@" --include=*.gab` is
-- empty). It was a promise nobody keeps, and it looked kept.
--
-- WHY THE REFUSAL AND NOT THE PASS
-- --------------------------------
-- The mark would mean *"the target is owned, and the owning mark is `m`"* -- a
-- statement about linearity the checker would have to hold at every call site.
-- Rule A: a construct without a measured need is not built. Saying so by name
-- costs nothing and stops the silence. The refusal prints the repair: write
-- `own`, and name the owner where the language does hold it, in
-- `effects { consumes m }`.
--
-- AT THE SIGNATURE, NOT AT THE ACCESS («W10»)
-- --------------------------------------------
-- A body that takes the pointer and never touches it is refused too -- coarser
-- than the defect, and coarse in the safe direction. The exact rule would need
-- the mark at every access site, and the expression lowering does not carry it.
-- The `ptr<port, …>` refusal directly above it in `emit.rs` makes the same cut
-- for the same reason.
module gift::eigentumsmarke {

linear ghost type Besitz;

type Zelle = { wert : u32, };

impl fn lies(p : ptr<normal, own@Besitz> Zelle) -> u32
    effects { reads p }
    costs   <= 2 ops
{
    return p->wert;
}

}
